From 5943e52cec2bee678b1057fb5d257bba8906518f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:46:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: restrict provider families
X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: provider-family model and completion allowlist
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-provider-policy
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1002-personal-openrouter-eu.patch

Patch intent:
Add [provider].allowed_providers to hide disallowed provider-family models and
block their use.

Why it exists:
Keeps sessions inside an explicit provider allowlist while preserving empty-list
legacy behavior.

Upstream integration points:
Catalogs, model switching, completion, fallback, and endpoint details project
provider-family policy.

Update guidance:
Keep route-family mapping exhaustive, including openrouter-eu as a distinct
family.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-base provider_route_ --lib
